 "segments": [
  "[  0.00-  4.24] Gambling is illegal in Japan, yet there's a gambling hall on almost every street.",
  "[  4.50-  9.30] Inside, thousands of machines are flashing and screaming while people carry out buckets full",
  "[  9.30- 13.86] of steel balls. Police stroll right past the door, but nobody ever gets arrested. So,",
  "[ 14.12- 18.38] you win a bucket yourself and try to cash it in, but the counter won't give you a single yen.",
  "[ 18.66- 23.62] Instead, you can pick cookies, chocolate, a bottle of shampoo, or a few tiny plastic tokens.",
  "[ 23.92- 27.32] The guy in front of you takes the tokens and heads straight outside. You follow him",
  "[ 27.32- 30.58] around the corner to a little window in a wall with no sign. You see,",
  "[ 30.86- 34.94] that window isn't part of the gambling hall. It's technically a separate shop that just",
  "[ 34.94- 38.80] happens to buy those exact tokens. So, the hall only ever gives out prizes,",
  "[ 39.12- 41.84] and the shop is just buying one. He slides the tokens through,",
  "[ 42.12- 45.02] a hand slides over cash, and on paper, nobody gambles."
 ],
